       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Confirming the dose doesn't change the problem. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is well beyond the maximum of 10 mg per day. It carries a real risk of severe hypotension and shock, and it can cause delayed, prolonged toxicity because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours. You haven't given a clinical reason for it, and I can't think of a standard indication for it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily, or 10 mg if you want the maximum. I can do either right now.\n- **Get a second check.** If you think an unusual dose is warranted, please talk to your attending and the pharmacist first. They can enter or co-sign the order through the proper channel.\n- **Check for a slip.** If this came from a template, a transcription, or a handoff, it may be an error that needs correcting at the source.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
